1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,505
Why does a no-smoking plane toilet have an

2
00:00:02,505 --> 00:00:03,205
ashtray?

3
00:00:03,695 --> 00:00:05,618
Smoking on every US flight has been banned

4
00:00:05,618 --> 00:00:08,541
since 2000... yet the rules still demand

5
00:00:08,541 --> 00:00:10,618
an ashtray on every toilet door.

6
00:00:10,946 --> 00:00:12,611
Because the real danger isn't the smoker.

7
00:00:12,965 --> 00:00:14,628
It's where the cigarette ends up.

8
00:00:14,965 --> 00:00:16,696
Someone who breaks the rule panics and

9
00:00:16,696 --> 00:00:18,658
hides it, and the nearest hiding spot is

10
00:00:18,658 --> 00:00:20,254
a bin full of paper towels.

11
00:00:20,553 --> 00:00:22,437
So the rule gives them one obvious, safe

12
00:00:22,437 --> 00:00:23,803
place to put it out first.

13
00:00:24,102 --> 00:00:25,929
That bin even has its own tiny fire

14
00:00:25,929 --> 00:00:27,929
extinguisher, and a smoke detector watches

15
00:00:27,929 --> 00:00:28,629
the room.

16
00:00:28,843 --> 00:00:31,247
So this ashtray isn't for smokers...

17
00:00:31,247 --> 00:00:32,689
it's for the fire nobody wants.
